    "title": "What channel is NY Mets vs Diamondbacks today? How to watch, prediction",
    "text": "Updated April 7, 2026, 2:32 p.m. ETThe New York Mets (6-4, 1st in NL East) are back home as they get ready for a six-game homestand that begins with a three-game series versus the Arizona Diamondbacks (5-5, 2nd in NL West) on Tuesday at Citi Field.The Mets are coming off a seven-game road trip in which they went 4-3 and are currently on a three-game winning streak after taking three of four against the San Francisco Giants.The news isn't all positive, as Mets star outfielder Juan Soto landed on the 10-day injured list and is expected to miss two to three weeks with a right calf strain.Soto's absence leaves a huge hole in the Mets starting lineup, as Carson Benge and Tyrone Taylor are just a couple of options to replace the four-time All-Star in the outfield over the next few weeks.Here's how to watch, the updated first pitch time due to cold weather, and our prediction for the Mets vs. Diamondbacks series opener in Queens on Tuesday:What is new start time for NY Mets vs Diamondbacks game today?Time: 4:10 p.m.With cold weather on the horizon over the next few days, the Mets moved up Tuesday's and Wednesday's start times, which were originally scheduled for 7:10 p.m., to first pitch now coming at 4:10 p.m. for both games.What is weather forecast for NY Mets vs Diamondbacks game today?Here's the weather forecast for today's series opener between the Mets and Diamondbacks, according to weather.com:Tuesday night: Mostly clear skies with a low of 33 degrees. Winds NNW at 15 to 25 mph.What channel is NY Mets vs Diamondbacks today?TV: SNYHow to stream NY Mets vs Diamondbacks game todayStreaming: MLB.TV for out of market viewersNY Mets, Diamondbacks starting pitchers todayMets: Freddy Peralta (1-0, 4.35 ERA)Diamondbacks: Zac Gallen (1-1, 3.60 ERA)Mets ace Freddy Peralta was much sharper in his second start with the team, as he struck out seven and allowed just one run on three hits in 5 1/3 innings of work but was tagged with a no-decision.It's a similar story for Diamondbacks ace Zac Gallen. The Somerdale, New Jersey, native struggled against the World Series champion Los Angeles Dodgers on Opening Day. Gallen bounced back in his most recent outing, as he pitched six shutout innings and picked up his first win of the season.NY Mets vs Diamondbacks odds for today's gameOdds according to BetMGM as of Tuesday, April 7:Spread: Mets by 1.5Over/under: 7Moneyline: Mets (-160), Diamondbacks (+135)Prediction for Mets vs Diamondbacks todayIt's a pitching duel at Citi Field, as neither offense can sustain much success at the plate with Peralta and Gallen dueling in Queens.Tied late, the Mets take the lead in the latter innings and hold on for good to win the series opener and extend their winning streak to four games.Mets 3, Diamondbacks 2",
